 ### Priority
 
@@ -118,6 +118,13 @@ ### Ordering and Fairness
 
 The **next candidate queue** is **deterministic**: same state input → same next ticket, no random draw.
 
+**Implementation** (`App\Actions\CallNextTicket`):
+
+- A ticket is **normal** when `priority = 0` and **priority** when `priority > 0`.
+- Only `waiting` tickets of the given queue are candidates.
+- Ordering: higher `priority` first, then oldest `issued_at`, then lowest `id`.
+- **Fairness (`any` mode only):** look at the last 3 tickets called in the queue (most recent first by `called_at`, then `id`). If there are 3, all are priority, and at least one normal ticket is waiting, only normal tickets are considered (the oldest normal is called). Calls made in `priority_only`/`normal_only` mode count in this history; a normal call resets the streak. If no normal is waiting, priority tickets keep being called.
+
 ### Call Panel (attendant)
 
 Three explicit actions, all deterministic:
@@ -128,6 +135,10 @@ ### Call Panel (attendant)
 | **Priority** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among priority candidates (includes 80+ per configuration). |
 | **Normal** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among normal candidates. |
 
+Modes (`App\Enums\CallMode`): `any` (Next: full ordering + fairness), `priority_only` (only priority tickets, full ordering, fairness ignored) and `normal_only` (only normal tickets, oldest first, fairness ignored).
+
+`App\Actions\CallNextTicket` is invoked as `(new CallNextTicket)($queue, $calledBy, CallMode::Any)` and returns the updated ticket. Calling from an inactive queue throws `InactiveQueueException` and changes nothing (queue state is read from the database under lock, not from the passed model). When no ticket is eligible for the mode (empty queue, only normals in `priority_only`, only priority in `normal_only`) it throws `NoWaitingTicketsException`. Authorization (who may call) is **not** checked by the action; the caller is trusted.
+
 After each call, the ticket leaves the waiting queue and enters the session/display call history.
 
